# Where `kdos app update` looks, one directory per line.
#
# A source is a directory with a `PACKAGES` index in it — not a URL. The
# medium kdos-packd reports is always consulted and does not need a line here;
# this file is for a second stick, a mounted share, or a directory somebody
# rsync'd a repository into.
#
# The index is what says which packs exist and what their payload hashes are.
# Nothing here is trusted: kdos-packd hashes and verifies every pack where the
# mount happens, so a source can offer a file and still not get it installed.
#
# /mnt/usb/packs
